Which agent gets an order is a policy that changes with business needs — a **Strategy**, swappable without touching `Order` or `OrderState`.

```text
interface AgentAssignmentStrategy:
    method assignAgent(order: Order): DeliveryAgent

class NearestAgentStrategy implements AgentAssignmentStrategy:
    method assignAgent(order): DeliveryAgent:
        candidates = agentPool.filter(a -> a.isAvailable)
        if candidates.isEmpty():
            throw NoAgentAvailableException()
        return candidates.minBy(a -> distance(a.currentLocation, order.restaurant.location))

class LeastBusyAgentStrategy implements AgentAssignmentStrategy:
    method assignAgent(order): DeliveryAgent:
        candidates = agentPool.filter(a -> a.isAvailable)
        if candidates.isEmpty():
            throw NoAgentAvailableException()
        return candidates.minBy(a -> a.activeOrderCount)
```

Nearest minimizes pickup time per order; least-busy spreads load evenly across agents. Production systems often blend both into a weighted score.
